cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyinfluence in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "pyinfluence: training data attribution for scikit-learn"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Schulz
    given-names: Marc-Andre
    email: marc.a.schulz@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/maschulz/pyinfluence"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-07-15
abstract: >-
  Training data attribution for scikit-learn estimators: closed-form
  influence functions, exact leave-one-out retraining, Data Banzhaf and
  bootstrap out-of-bag estimators, and a functional-influence engine that
  attributes scalar model properties (fairness disparities, AUROC,
  worst-group loss) to individual training examples.
